THE MIT GRANT ABOVE COVERS THIS PROJECT'S ORIGINAL CODE ONLY:

    redetail.py   build_ui_workflow.py   tools/   demos/

IT DOES NOT COVER THE MODEL WEIGHTS, IT DOES NOT COVER THE WORKFLOW FILES IN
workflows/, AND IT DOES NOT COVER THE CACHED CONDITIONING TENSORS IN
tools/comfyui_cond_cache/ (*.pt). Those are governed by the LTX-2 Community
License Agreement, a complete copy of which is included at:

    workflows/LICENSE-LTX-2-Community.txt

as required by section 3(b) of that Agreement.


THE WORKFLOW FILES ARE MODIFIED DERIVATIVES
-------------------------------------------
workflows/ReDetail_LTX25_upscale.json and workflows/ltx25_upscale_API.json are
DERIVED, WITH MODIFICATIONS, from Lightricks' shipped example

    example_workflows/2.5/LTX-2.5_V2V_ICLoRA_Single_Stage_Distilled.json
    github.com/Lightricks/ComfyUI-LTXVideo

Changes made (section 3(c) requires this notice): model filenames repointed to
the int8_convrot quantisation, the IC-LoRA swapped from instant-shave to the
pixel spatial upscaler, two canvas links severed so the output dimensions are
settable, the reference-resize default changed, a placeholder image set, and
six documentation panels rewritten. build_ui_workflow.py performs and documents
every one of these edits.

Lightricks' unmodified example is NOT redistributed here. Fetch it from the
repository above; build_ui_workflow.py prints the exact path if it is absent.

These files are distributed EXCLUSIVELY under the LTX-2 Community License
Agreement, per section 3(b). The MIT grant above does not apply to them.


THE CACHED CONDITIONING TENSORS ARE MODEL OUTPUT
------------------------------------------------
tools/comfyui_cond_cache/redetail_pos.pt and redetail_neg.pt are the OUTPUT of
Lightricks' LTX-2.5 text encoder, specifically

    gemma4-12b-with-proj-ltx-2.5-Q5_K_M.gguf  (type ltxv)

encoding the empty string. Each is a single float32 tensor of shape (1, 1, 6144)
and roughly 26 KB. They exist because this graph's prompt boxes are empty, which
makes that conditioning a constant, so shipping it means the text encoder never
has to be downloaded or loaded at all.

Being derived from the LTX-2.5 weights, they are treated here as material
governed by the LTX-2 Community License Agreement rather than by the MIT grant,
and the same use restrictions and commercial terms carry forward to you.

They are quantisation-specific in origin: the int8_convrot encoder is a
different quantisation of the same model, and its embedding of the empty string
has NOT been verified byte-identical to these. It is expected to be numerically
close. If you would rather not rely on that, regenerate them yourself with

    python3 redetail.py --bootstrap-cond --encoder <your encoder>

which writes to ComfyUI/output/cond_cache/ and takes precedence over these.


THE WEIGHTS
-----------
  * LTX-2.5 (Lightricks) ............... LTX-2 Community License Agreement
  * LTX-2.5 IC-LoRA Pixel Spatial
    Upscaler (Lightricks) .............. see that model repository's own terms

Both Hugging Face repositories are gated and require accepting their licence.


